# The byte content of these files *is* the evidence: every one of them is pinned by a
# published SHA-256 (see README.md). Git must therefore never normalise their line
# endings.
#
# The export writes them with CRLF (Python text mode on Windows). With
# `core.autocrlf=true` and no attribute, the committed blob would be LF, so a fresh
# clone would reproduce different bytes and none of the published hashes would verify -
# exactly what C caught on the first delivery (`4142a248...` committed vs the published
# `75caedb8...` for 600519 normalized).
*.json -text

# Same reason as `docs/evidence/c-delivery/`: CRLF bytes would otherwise make
# `git diff --check` report one "trailing whitespace" finding per line, burying real
# whitespace problems. Scoped to these paths only; a CR at end of line is part of the
# terminator here. This changes no file's bytes.
*.json whitespace=cr-at-eol
